  "limits": [
    "The sampler observes only these bounded benchmark windows; it is not full acquisition/public-HTTPS or continuous lifetime resource coverage.",
    "The benchmark reads whole kernel records into 2 MiB of prefaulted memory, then persists after measurements. Sampler memory/CPU is excluded from worker accounting but can affect scheduling and pressure.",
    "Kernel signature scans are literal diagnostics, not proof that all errors are absent and not causal attribution of latency. Raw logs and identities remain private.",
    "Four measured pairs per TV are too few to characterize tails; these comparisons do not close the no-regression gate. Earlier one-second job admissions and the historical QN90A timeout remain unexplained.",
    "Original sync attribution and this non-interposed capture are separate trials; no individual sync latency is inferred from this capture.",
    "No package, power or policy change was issued. Unexpected boot changes occurred between qualification windows; they are not controlled reboot acceptance. Managed fallback and independent .NET SDK recovery remain installed."
  ]
